{"description":"`eka status` execution section can display `eka` repository execution state while running inside another registered project. `cmd/status.go` first searches current project, but fallback unconditionally resolves `eka/ses:execution-state`. If project lookup fails or has no local SES, output leaks the legacy EKA state instead of remaining project-scoped.","impact":"Operators and agents see wrong active container, current item, next item, and execution mode. This can cause execution against the wrong project.","acceptanceCriteria":"- Resolve execution state by current repository ProjectID and namespace.\n- If no project-local SES exists, show no execution state or an explicit project-scoped not-found result; never silently use another project's state.\n- Preserve legacy fallback only when current repository itself is the legacy EKA project.\n- Add tests with two registered projects and distinct `ses:execution-state` records.\n- `eka status` output matches current project only."}